            <div xml:id="d778">

                <pb facs="0820" n="718" sameAs="frus:frus1933v03/pg718"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">393.1111 M Nielsen, Niels/4: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Minister in China (Johnson) to the Secretary of
                        State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Peiping</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1933-04-17T17:00:00+08:00">April 17, 1933—5
                        p.m.</date><lb/>[Received April 17—5 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>334. My 324, April 13, 5 p.m. Following from American Consul General at Mukden:
                        <quote rend="blockquote">
                        <p>“April 16, 9 a.m. Japanese military report that Nielsen was kidnapped by
                            bandits under Liu Ching-wen, a former magistrate and that he is believed
                            to be at a hamlet southwest of Siuyen.”</p>
                    </quote></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Johnson</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
